# LF everywhere, on every OS: the shell scripts run under bash (also Git Bash on Windows, issue #49) and on the Echo's
# mksh, and device.conf, *.rc, sepolicy.rules and the rest are sourced or pushed to it as they are.  A Windows clone
# with Git's default core.autocrlf=true got CRLF, and bash fails on that.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.raw binary
*.mp3 binary
# the speech corpus's clips (tools/speechcorpus, 500 MB) in Git LFS: a clone and CI's checkout (no lfs: true) get
# pointers only; `git lfs pull --include "testdata/corpus/**"` fetches them
testdata/corpus/**/*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
